                <pb facs="0556" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 15778/70A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 181.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence in the
                    matter of the murder of Charles Rand and the wounding of Joseph Cieslik, members
                    of the crew of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Buffalo</hi>, at Panama, on
                    September 28, 1908, and especially to the department’s instruction of October
                    23, 1908, I have to instruct you to ascertain what steps are being taken by the
                    Government of Panama to meet the demands upon it contained in the instruction of
                    October 23, 1908, above referred to.</p>
                <p>The department considers the outrage to the sailors of the United States and the
                    insult to this Government as serious as when they occurred in September, 1908,
                    and fears that delay in the matter may cause Panama to overlook either the
                    seriousness or the necessity of making complete and adequate satisfaction to the
                    dead and injured and to their Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
